WEBVTT

00:03:28.954 --> 00:03:31.413
so we can really track where people moved.

00:03:31.454 --> 00:03:34.954
And we've looked at this
for hundreds and thousands of individuals

00:03:34.996 --> 00:03:36.746
to identify migration in the past.

00:03:36.788 --> 00:03:39.704
So I'd like to introduce you
to some ancient migrants.

00:03:39.746 --> 00:03:43.329
If we go back in time 1600 years,
we can go to the city of Copán,

00:03:43.371 --> 00:03:46.079
where the Maya people lived
in what's now Honduras.

00:03:46.121 --> 00:03:48.454
If we came around the year 400 AD,

00:03:48.496 --> 00:03:51.829
we might have walked into broad plazas
under a really hot tropical sun

00:03:51.871 --> 00:03:54.329
that was shining
onto bright red-painted buildings

00:03:54.371 --> 00:03:56.996
that had altars and carved statues
in front of them.

00:03:57.038 --> 00:03:58.704
If we'd come on the right day,

00:03:58.746 --> 00:04:02.454
we might have seen the inauguration
of ruler K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo',